---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import TrustBar from '../components/TrustBar.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import Needed from '../components/Needed.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/site.js';
import { client } from '../data/client.js';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: client.owner.name,
  jobTitle: client.owner.role,
  worksFor: { '@id': `${client.url}/#business` },
};
---
<Layout
  path="/about/"
  title="About Swift Electrical & Security"
  description="Swift Electrical & Security is run by Adil, a NICEIC registered electrician working across Bradford and West Yorkshire. Who turns up, what the registration actually means, and how we price the work."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
  schemas={[personSchema]}
>
  <Hero inner={true}>
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Who you're dealing with, and what he's registered to do.</h1>
    <p class="hero__sub">
      Swift Electrical &amp; Security is a NICEIC registered electrician and
      security installer run by Adil, working across Bradford and West
      Yorkshire.
    </p>
  </Hero>

  <div class="container"><TrustBar /></div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="frame reveal">
        <Placeholder
          src={client.owner.photo}
          alt={`${client.owner.name}, ${client.name}`}
          label="Photo of Adil needed"
          hint="Real photo, not stock. There are 18 posts on the Instagram already — a still from one of those would do to start."
          variant="ph--portrait"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2>Adil</h2>
        <p class="lead">{client.owner.bio}</p>
        <p class="muted">
          A landlord renewing EICRs on several properties says he struggled to
          find anyone at all, and that the firms he did find quoted extortionate
          prices. Another says Adil talked him through exactly what needed doing
          before doing any of it. Three of the seven Google reviews name him.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          The security side is half the business and it's in the name. Two of
          the seven reviews are about camera installs, one from a customer who
          has used the company several times.
        </p>
        <div class="ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;padding:24px;margin-top:22px;text-align:left">
          <strong>Adil's own words needed here</strong>
          <small>
            How he got into the trade, what he did before, why he added security
            to the electrical side. Two or three paragraphs, first person, in
            his voice. This is the highest-trust content on the site.
          </small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--panel">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__head reveal">
        <h2>What NICEIC registration actually means</h2>
        <p>
          NAPIT has told Parliament that public awareness of the competent-person
          schemes is low. Ask ten people what NICEIC registration involves and
          you'll get ten shrugs, so we've written down what it buys you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="creds">
        <div class="cred reveal">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="shield" /></span>
          <h3>NICEIC registered</h3>
          <p>
            An independent assessor inspects our work every year. Registration
            also lets us self-certify to Building Control, so you get the
            compliance certificate your solicitor asks for the day you sell.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:12px"><Needed label="ENROLMENT NUMBER — so you can check the register" /></p>
        </div>

        <div class="cred reveal" style="transition-delay:80ms">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="clipboard" /></span>
          <h3>Certified and notified</h3>
          <p>
            Everything gets tested to BS 7671. "Notifiable" means a new circuit,
            a board change or anything in a bathroom, and the law puts that
            paperwork on you, the homeowner. We file it, so it exists.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cred reveal" style="transition-delay:160ms">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="check" /></span>
          <h3>Qualifications</h3>
          <p>We list the tickets behind the work so you can check them instead of taking them on trust.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:12px"><Needed label="2391? 18th Edition? ECS card?" /></p>
        </div>

        <div class="cred reveal" style="transition-delay:240ms">
          <span class="cred__ico"><Icon name="star" /></span>
          <h3>Insured</h3>
          <p>We state the public liability figure. "Fully insured" on its own tells you nothing.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:12px"><Needed label="COVER AMOUNT" /></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="inline-cta reveal">
        <p>Want the numbers before you book? Ask and we'll send them over.</p>
        <a class="btn btn--act" href={href('/contact/')}>Ask us <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow reveal">
      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>
        Testing and fixing are two different jobs, and we keep them that way.
        You hear what we found and what it will cost before anything starts.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        We won't tell you something is urgent when it isn't. An old fuse board
        is worth knowing about, and it is almost never an emergency, whatever
        the last person through your door told you. Get a second opinion. We
        would rather you did that than take our word for it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand title="Want a price?" />
</Layout>

<style>
  li { display: flex; gap: 13px; align-items: flex-start; }
  li svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; color: var(--brand); flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 4px; }
  li strong { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); margin-bottom: 3px; }
  li span { color: var(--muted); }
  li strong { color: var(--text); }
</style>
